--><gorp name="T02 Data Instance"><!-- nos-uml-state {"mode":"ai-design","title":"T02 Data Instance","layout":{"ut.data.Reading":{"x":60,"y":60,"w":280,"h":140},"ut.data.Sample":{"x":60,"y":260,"w":280,"h":140},"ut.data.Report":{"x":420,"y":60,"w":280,"h":140},"ut.data.Summary":{"x":780,"y":60,"w":280,"h":140}}} --><comment view="class">Adds real values to T01's shape. The data node Sample is an INSTANCE of the model Reading (of=), so it carries one row per model row with a value in it — 3 counts and 1.75 m — and a Run has something to send as inputs.

count is an integer and Sums; level is a real and takes Monotone. A data node is the only place a value belongs; a model row declares shape only.</comment><expect>Check finds nothing. Run sends inputs keyed Reading.count and Reading.level and comes back OK.

Clear either value and Check must name it — "Sample.count — value is empty" — and grey the Run button. An empty value is an error, not a default.</expect><model namespace="ut.data.Reading"><variables><variable name="count" type="int" collapse="Sum"><unit basis="\one" namespace="D-SI" /></variable><variable name="level" type="double" collapse="Monotone"><unit basis="\metre" namespace="D-SI" /></variable></variables></model><data namespace="ut.data.Sample" of="ut.data.Reading"><variables><variable name="count" type="int" collapse="Sum">3<unit basis="\one" namespace="D-SI" /></variable><variable name="level" type="double" collapse="Monotone">1.75<unit basis="\metre" namespace="D-SI" /></variable></variables></data><algorithm namespace="ut.data.Report"><input model="ut.data.Reading" /><output model="ut.data.Summary" /><operations><operation name="report" returns="double" /></operations></algorithm><model namespace="ut.data.Summary"><variables><variable name="total" type="double" collapse="Monotone"><unit basis="\metre" namespace="D-SI" /></variable></variables></model></gorp>